e\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"dea1e2308f69\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Any obvious physical signs, like not breathing or not having a pulse\"]}]]}]\n66:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12418d967295\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"The treatments for shock can vary slightly depending on which type of shock you’re experiencing. But when someone’s unconscious, all shock treatments start with the ABCs. Those letters stand for:\"]}]\n67:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"4220704478a3-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"4220704478a3\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"7504f463193f\",{\"children\":[\"Airway\"]}],\": Make sure their airway is open and clear, and tilt their chin up slightly to keep it open.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"fbcbc6955549\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"c32aed47f437\",{\"children\":[\"Breathing\"]}],\": Check if they’re breathing or not.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"526553028ff8\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"df3b4f7d0fcf\",{\"children\":[\"Circulation\"]}],\": Make sure blood can circulate.\"]}]]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"p\",\"e4c3d15e5f99\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"It’s absolutely critical to confirm these in that order. That’s because you can’t survive more than a few minutes if you aren’t breathing, and you can’t breathe if your airway is blocked.\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"6cc6e35d4df2\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:fon"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"t-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"If they’re breathing\"]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3e3835158938\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"If the person is breathing, look for any potential threats to their circulation. If they have severe bleeding, try the following measures (if one doesn’t work, move on to the next):\"]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"9fa7230616fe-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"ordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-rem24px list-decimal marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal marker:text-brandBlue-500 marker:font-semibold print:marker:text-black  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"9fa7230616fe\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"e0200ac9b5a6\",{\"children\":[\"Apply direct pressure\"]}],\": Put a bandage on the wound and press directly on the wound. Don’t hesitate to press hard, even if it’s painful. Maintain that pressure until first responders arrive.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"bcddb2d5f178\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"d9fec02d7e26\",{\"children\":[\"Pack the wound\"]}],\": Use gauze or bandage material and push it into the wound. Then, apply direct pressure on top of the wound itself. In an emergency, a towel or T-shirt works, too. Stopping the bleeding is more important than worrying about infection right now.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"11cbd7c42e30\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"f89564d2b8c0\",{\"children\":[\"Use a cinching method like a Spanish windlass (for wounds on limbs only)\"]}],\": Tie a bandage loosely around the wound and insert a rod or stick just underneath. Wind the object so the bandage cinches tightly atop the wound. Once the bleeding stops, tie the winding object in place.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5f70606627d8\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 mb-rem12px text-rem19px leading-rem34px pl-rem12px print:mb-rem4px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1961906c7d3c\",{\"children\":[\"Use a \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"553b00a61ad1\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/tourniquet\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"tourniquet\"]}],\" (for wounds on limbs only)\"]}],\": This stops bleeding by cutting off blood flow to the injury. You should only use this as a last resort or if you need to quickly stop bleeding so you can do other lifesaving care like CPR.\"]}]]}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"div\",\"5f70606627d8_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard3_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"486153db1652\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8px  \",\"children\":[\"If they’re not breathing\"]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4dd431096d80\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"If the person isn’t breathing, the circulation step often means starting \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"6fa52420c43a\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/17680-cardiopulmonary-resuscitation-cpr\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"CPR\"]}],\". But if the person has severe bleeding, you have to stop the bleeding immediately so they’ll have as much blood left in their body to circulate as possible. Once you \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1637ac7c64f2\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://health.clevelandclinic.org/how-to-stop-bleeding\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"stop the bleeding\"]}],\", you can then start CPR.\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"40df1b772298\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Keep doing CPR until you can get an automated external \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"0a248f81eb89\",{\"data-identity\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/treatments/23020-defibrillator\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"className\":\"text-brandBlue-500 print:text-black underline underline-offset-[5px] print:no-underline decoration-1 break-words hover:text-blue-800 transition\",\"children\":[\"defibrillator\"]}],\" (AED) and try to use it. If you don’t have or can’t use an AED, continue CPR until help arrives. Remember, CPR is very tiring. Swap out with others who can also do CPR when you need to rest.\"]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"h4\",\"fcee8d0f09dc\",{\"data-identity\":\"headline\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"text-gray-900 font-bold leading-rem24px text-rem20px bp600:text-rem25px bp600:leading-rem30px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-bold mt-rem32px mb-rem16px break-words print:mt-rem12px print:text-rem19px print:leading-rem27px print:font-semibold print:mb-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Other things you can do to help someone in shock\"]}]\n71:[\"$\",\"p\",\"d155e6c805bf\",{\"data-identity\":\"paragraph-element\",\"className\":\"text-gray-800 my-rem16px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal print:my-rem8px  \",\"children\":[\"Some other key actions you can take to help someone in shock or in danger of going into shock are:\"]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"258aa67f33f0-parent\",{\"data-identity\":\"unordered-list\",\"className\":\"my-rem16px mx-0 pl-[1.25rem] list-disc marker:text-brandBlue-500 print:marker:text-black marker:pl-rem24px print:my-rem8px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal  \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"258aa67f33f0\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"cccffb954a35\",{\"children\":[\"Keep them warm\"]}],\": Use blankets or jackets to cover them.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5cfa39b47e3a\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"7794a23a3ba3\",{\"children\":[\"Elevate their feet by about 12 inches \"]}],\"(unless they might have a head, neck, back, hip or leg injury): This helps push blood toward their torso and head. That can make it easier to circulate blood to critical organs like the brain. Don’t elevate their head.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"147a84715d54\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"433d74de90"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"80\",{\"children\":[\"Treat specific causes\"]}],\": If a person is in shock because of an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis, see if they have something like an epinephrine auto-injector.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"7b1d7626e9fc\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem19px leading-rem34px print:text-rem15px print:leading-rem20px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"346805c9e43e\",{\"children\":[\"Use the rescue position if needed\"]}],\": If they start to vomit, drool or bleed from their mouth, put them in the recovery position. Keep their back, neck and head aligned, and gently roll them onto their side. Stretch out their arm nearest the ground and use it to support their head.\"]}]]}]\n73:[\"$\",\"div\",\"7b1d7626e9fc_mobile_ad\",{\"data-identity\":\"billboard-ad\",\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden print:hidden max-w-[400px] min-w-[300px] m-auto items-center justify-center bg-gray-300 pt-rem16px pb-[3.125rem] my-rem32px  \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-[300px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 uppercase text-rem10px leading-rem16px mx-auto w-fit\",\"children\":\"Advertisement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex bp1100:hidden flex-col items-center justify-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-identity\":\"ad-slot\",\"id\":\"billboard4_300x250_mobile\",\"className\":\"ad-reset w-[300px] !min-h-[250px] flex bg-gray-300\"}],null]}]]}]}]\n76:[\"$\",\"span\",\"2a9b8f132e67\",{\"className\":\"break-words\",\"children\":[[\"Shock\"],[\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":[\"(\",\"https://www.emergencyphysicians.org/article/know-when-to-go/shock\",\")\"]}]]]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"li\",\"81691e966f0a\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem15px leading-rem19px marker:text-rem19px print:text-rem13px print:leading-rem16px print:font-normal \",\"children\":[\"Angus DC. Approach to the Patient with Shock. In: Goldman L, Cooney KA, eds. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"0b4072a46e88\",{\"children\":[\"Goldman-Cecil Medicine.\"]}],\" 27th ed. Elsevier Inc. 2024:658-665.\"]}]\n78:[\"$\",\"li\",\"67d97b07eee1\",{\"className\":\"mb-rem12px pl-rem12px text-gray-800 print:mb-rem4px text-rem15px leading-rem19px marker:text-rem19px print:text-rem13px print:leading-rem16px print:font-normal \",\"chil